Title: "States"
Id: "ece66d82-2933-4bb7-aa7a-74379dbc2001"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
[CommandHeader]
States: <OpenText>*
using?: <DeclarationStatement>+
when?: <ClauseUnion>+
that: <ClauseUnion>+
Requires?: <RequiresItemUnion>+
Enables?: <EnablesItemUnion>+
Documented?: <DocumentedItemUnion>+
Justification?: <HaveGroup>+
Aliases?: <AliasItemUnion>+
Writing?: \"<WritingAlias>\"+
References?: <ResourceHeader>+
Metadata?: <MetadataItemUnion>+
Id?: <OpenText>
```

`States:` introduces a named statement. `that:` is required and contains the
body of the statement.

```mlg-fragment
[\\commutative{S}]
States:
when: S is \\set
that:
. forAll: x, y is \\element.of{S}
  then:
  . x * y = y * x
Documented:
. called: \"commutative\"
Id: \"23e4567e-e89b-42d3-a456-426614174000\"
```

The `States:` section itself is required but may contain zero text entries.

`using:` introduces auxiliary symbols. `when:` states requirements for
command-header parameters. `Requires:` and `Enables:` describe capabilities that
the checker can use when resolving notation. `Documented:` must include at least
one of `called:` or `written:`. `Id:` is required for every top-level item;
`mlg check` adds it when missing."
Id: "3fdf0251-72f6-4154-bb2a-e7422ede6730"
